WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:02.640
<i>Haruto's been kidnapped!</i>

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:07.860
<i>While we were searching for Haruto, 
III and IV appeared before us!</i>

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:12.110
<i>Kaito, let's beat these guys down in a Tag Duel!</i>

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:14.820
<i>I will definitely bring Haruto back!</i>

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.240
<i>I'm gonna bring it to 'em!</i>

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.380
It's beautiful...!

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:30.170
So this is Astral World!

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:38.140
The time has finally come, Kaito...

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:48.230
Duel!!

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.940
Now, let's get my fanservice started!

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.700
Don't even joke with me...

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:58.660
And don't think you'll get out of this in one piece after laying your hands on Haruto.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.410
You sure are confident.

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:05.330
I'll give you the same loss I handed that one's friends!

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:09.540
I'm the one who's gonna beat you, IV!

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:11.880
Yuma, don't get worked up.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.050
It's part of his strategy.

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:18.010
I know that. I won't Duel for revenge!

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:24.270
Kaito-<i>sama</i>...

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:28.440
Hey! Sucky Foolma over there! You better not get in Kaito-<i>sama</i>'s way!

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:29.900
What's your problem?!

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:32.270
I said he sucks because he sucks!

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:33.900
Come again?!

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.860
Eeee...! Um...

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:40.120
I won't let you make fun of Yuma, you deadbeat!

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:42.370
D...deadbeat?

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:43.040
Hmph!

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:46.000
This girl might be even scarier than Kaito-<i>sama</i>...

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.210
Here goes! My turn! Draw!

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.710
I Summon Gimmick Puppet - Bomb Egg!

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:01.890
Bomb Egg's effect activates!

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:08.890
This Monster lets me send a card from hand once per turn to inflict 800 points of damage to my opponent.

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:10.230
Right off the bat?!

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:15.320
You aren't able to attack on the first turn of a Tag Duel, but Effect Damage is something else entirely.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:19.320
I send Gimmick Puppet - Necro Doll to the Graveyard!

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:25.490
Consider this my greeting. Accept it, Kaito!

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:34.000
Kaito!

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.670
You stay out of this!

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:38.130
Why should I? I'm worried about you, you know!

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:41.840
I set a card face-down and end my turn!

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:44.300
Now it's <i>your</i> turn.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:48.060
If you dillydally, there's no telling what will happen to Haruto.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:49.560
You monster...

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:52.060
My turn! Draw!

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:56.530
I activate the Field Magic, Photon Pressure World!

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:14.960
What the heck? Now we're in space?

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:16.420
That means...

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.050
I can't breath!

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.550
Calm down, Yuma.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:25.430
Then I Summon Photon Crusher!

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:33.440
And with the Field Magic, every player not controlling a Photon Monster

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:37.940
will take damage equal to the Photon Monster's level times 100.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:39.650
What?!

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:41.360
H-Hold on a minute!

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.740
I don't have Photon Monsters!

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:46.330
That means I'll take damage, doesn't it?!

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.660
I don't need your strength.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:49.290
Huh?

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:51.370
I will get Haruto back with my own hands.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:54.710
Take 400 points of damage!

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:08.390
You're supposed to be on Yuma's side, you know!

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:10.220
So you don't care about your comrades, huh?

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:12.850
Heh, I like that.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:16.020
I set a card face-down and end my turn.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:18.860
Kaito, why you...!

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:24.240
I understand. If that's how you're gonna be, then I'll do the same!

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:28.620
Wait, Yuma! We need to cooperate with Kaito if we want to win this Duel!

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:30.490
It's not my fault!

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:32.250
It's his fault, isn't it?!

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.290
Did you forget?

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:38.630
It's not just us riding on this Duel. Haruto's life is also in danger.

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:45.470
Haruto...

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:50.510
Looks like you don't know a thing.

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:52.020
Huh?

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:57.980
Kaito, you're a pitiful soldier working for Haruto's sake.

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:05.280
You're collecting Numbers for Dr. Faker and Mr. Heartland so they'll cure Haruto's sickness, right?

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.160
I knew it...!

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:12.660
You're gathering Numbers to cure Haruto's sickness!

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:18.040
<i>To save my brother, I sold my soul to the devil.</i>

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:25.720
That's right! He struggled to gather Numbers for Haruto's sake!

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:28.680
All without giving a damn about the souls of strangers!

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:30.720
What a touching story!

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:31.970
I can feel the tears coming.

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:35.390
Be quiet.

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:39.350
Why, Kaito...? Why didn't you tell me that?

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:41.980
I don't need your pity!

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:46.190
Anyone holding a Number will be hunted by me one of these days.

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:48.820
You and every one of them will...

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:52.830
Kaito... You...

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:57.410
I like, I like! Chase 'em all down, Kaito!

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:05.300
Healing Haruto... But that means that if we collect the Numbers, Haruto will...

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:08.470
Yuma, just concentrate on the fight right now.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:12.930
If we don't win this Duel right now, we won't be able to get Haruto back.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.310
Astral...

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:16.390
I understand.

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:18.810
My turn. Draw!

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:22.020
Brother, I'm going with the usual combo.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:26.820
I Summon OOPArts Golden Shuttle!

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:36.450
And then I activate the Magic Card, OOPArts Resonance!

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:42.170
This card lets me Special Summon an OOPArts Monster other than an

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:46.630
an OOPArts Monster on my field from my hand with a level one higher.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:50.760
I call forth the OOPArts Monster, Moai!

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:56.220
Then I activate Golden Shuttle's effect.

00:06:56.220 --> 00:07:00.310
I can increase the level of this card once per turn.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:04.190
Now he's got two Level Five Monsters.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:08.070
I Overlay the Level Five Golden Shuttle and Moai

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:11.660
I build the Overlay Network with my two Monsters!

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:19.120
Xyz Summon!

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:24.210
Show yourself, Number 33!

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:27.380
OOPArts Super Weapon - Machu Mach!

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:45.130
<i>As I get closer, I stretch my hand out</i>

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:48.180
<i>towards that shining light leading towards tomorrow</i>

00:07:48.350 --> 00:07:55.440
<i>I dream of a world that expands from my feet.</i>

00:07:59.190 --> 00:08:04.700
<i>I haven't a clue of where things like dreams and hopes are at.</i>

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:09.200
<i>Even if I run looking for it, I still can't seem to find it.</i>

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:15.660
<i>I wonder if I have fallen into a gap of truth and lies.</i>

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:20.460
<i>Even so, our grand tale has yet to begin.</i>

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:26.130
<i>Let's move on towards tomorrow, 
even if our road begins to fall apart.</i>

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:31.390
<i>I will jump forward, before all my
 strength completely drains.</i>

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:34.270
<i>The closer I get, the further it becomes,</i>

00:08:34.390 --> 00:08:37.560
<i>that truth that I must seize.</i>

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:42.730
<i>It's to find hope that we desire from a future unseen.</i>

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:45.320
<i>With a heart stronger than anyone else,</i>

00:08:45.530 --> 00:08:48.490
<i>I'll learn to keep running up.</i>

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:54.040
<i>With the strength to win any battle, 
despite just how weak I am,</i>

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:56.540
<i>My purpose is to find,</i>

00:08:56.540 --> 00:08:59.540
<i>with these invaluable friends of mine,</i>

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:06.340
<i>The future of the world expanding
 from my feet with my own eyes.</i>

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:16.700
I set 2 cards and end my turn!

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:20.830
L-Look at the size of that thing!

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:23.700
"Number 42: Yuma and Kaito: 
A Spirited Tag Duel"

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:24.910
Looks like they have more than more Number.

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:27.000
Don't let your guard down, Yuma!

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:28.750
I know!

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:32.630
My turn, draw!

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:35.300
I summon Ganbara Knight!

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:46.230
Next! When I normal summon a LV 4 monster to my field,

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:50.440
I can special summon this! 
Come, Kagetokage!

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:54.530
I'll gonna bring it to 'em!

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:59.070
I overlay my LV4 Ganbara Knight and Kagetokage!

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:06.410
I build the overlay network with these 2 monsters!

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:08.210
Xyz summon!

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:12.460
Oh? You were able to Xyz Summon, were you?

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:17.260
Come forth, Number 39: Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:26.980
What?!

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:27.850
A Number?!

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:33.900
That boy...

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:37.900
Impossible?! That brat... has a Number?

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:39.860
So he is a Numbers user.

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:44.240
Brother, maybe we were too negligent during the previous duels.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:47.120
He already has observed our duel once.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:49.250
Do we need to change the strategy?

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:51.250
Brother!

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:57.720
Now that's interesting!

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:01.550
It would be worthless to defeat someone without Numbers!

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.720
Yuma, set the card!

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:08.730
Both of them are Numbers users, and they are exceptionally strong!

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:13.150
This duel... we don't have luxury to hold back and not play the right card!

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:17.230
Right. I set 2 cards, and end my turn!

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:24.280
My turn, draw!

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:26.870
Now the show shall finally get started!

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:30.120
I activate the Magic card Level Cross!

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:33.960
With this card, I can send one card from my hand to the graveyard

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:37.130
to double the level of one LV4 or lower monster!

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:42.680
I send Gimmick Puppet Necro Doll to the graveyard, and double Bomb Egg's level!

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:47.600
Plus, since there are 2 Necro Dolls in my graveyard,

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:52.060
I can banish one of them, and special summon the other one!

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:02.780
There are 2 LV8 monsters!

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:05.200
So here it comes, that Numbers...

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:10.040
I overlay my LV8 Gimmick Puppet Bomb Egg and Necro Doll!

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:19.380
I build the overlay network with these 2 monsters!

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:21.420
Xyz summon!

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:27.640
Come forth, Number 15: Gimmick Puppet - Giant Killer!

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:41.320
That thing!

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:43.110
A Rank 8 Number!

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:45.910
I can't believe it would appear so quickly!

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:47.570
That monster...

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:51.750
...did something so brutal to Tetsuo-<i>kun</i> and the class president.

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:58.500
I activate the Permanent Trap Numbers Wall!

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:01.710
As long as card exists,

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:07.390
The Numbers on my field cannot be destroyed by the effects of Magic, traps or monsters!

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:12.350
An exclusive trap for Numbers!

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:14.310
Cannot be destroyed by card effects means...

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:15.770
Yuma, that's bad!

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:18.810
Let me tell you now.

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:22.110
I activate Giant Killer's effect!

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:28.820
By detaching one overlay unit, it will destroy all Xyz monsters except this card!

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:39.130
That way... his Number also won't be destroyed?

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:41.550
You fool!

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:46.840
Since my Number is protected by Numbers Wall, it will not be destroyed.

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:55.520
I am afraid that trap just now is a combo after foreseeing Giant Killer's effect!

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:56.890
That is...

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:01.860
We just fell into the trap set by those 2!

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:05.570
I can't use Hope's effect?!

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:06.570
It's no use.

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:12.990
Moon barrier can only be activated in response to attacks.

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:20.500
HOPE!

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:27.300
And Giant Killer will inflict damage equal to the ATK of the destroyed monsters,

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:30.470
to the player who controlled the respective monster!

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:43.110
Yuma!

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:49.780
That's bad! Giant Killer's ATK is 1500,

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:54.790
and it hasn't attacked yet! 
If we take that hit...

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:56.370
Darn!

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:59.160
Yuma, special summon Damage Mage!

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:01.130
I... I know!

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:04.290
I special summon Damage Mage in defense position!

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:12.430
This card can be special summoned when I take effect damage.

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:17.060
Then I recover life points equal to the amount of effect damage I took!

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:21.980
So you recovered your Life Points? How boring...

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:25.610
In that case, I activate the Magic card Attack Gimmick!

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:34.830
Due to this effect, until the end phase, Giant Killer gains 500 ATK.

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:41.920
Plus, when the targeted monster destroys a monster by battle,

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:46.800
it inflicts damage equal to the destroyed monster's ATK to my opponent!

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:50.050
Get ready, Kaito, you're first!

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:55.550
Giant Killer, attack Kaito's Photon Crusher!

00:15:57.510 --> 00:16:00.680
Why? The same attack should cause both of them to die!

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:02.980
Giant Killer is a Number.

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:04.980
It cannot be destroyed by this battle.

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:08.190
Final Dance!

00:16:09.230 --> 00:16:12.740
Alright, take that 2000 damage, Kaito!

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:23.170
Kaito!

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:28.750
Kaito-<i>sama</i>!

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:36.260
Can you still hunt my soul with the way you are right now, Kaito?

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:46.270
I just activated the Trap card Unrivaled Attack!

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:47.810
What did you say?

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:53.820
Unrivaled Attack: In battle with its effect it can prevent destruction!

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:58.700
As long as Photon Crusher is not destroyed, Kaito won't be damaged!

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:02.620
So your set card was to protect Kaito?

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:03.620
I end my turn!

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:08.630
Do you... really plan to protect me?

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:11.000
That's not what I meant!

00:17:11.670 --> 00:17:14.930
What's that person's problem?! Yuma just helped him!

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:18.680
I am sorry, that's the kind of person Kaito-<i>sama</i> is.

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:22.020
I already said it once. I don't need your strength.

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:24.850
Anyone who possesses Numbers is my enemy!

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:28.400
That's right. Is that Astral's order?

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:30.650
No, that was up to my own discretion!

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:34.110
If you treat me as your enemy, then I will be your enemy!

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:37.450
But I already promised Haruto.

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:40.330
He really desires to meet you!

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:43.790
Therefore, I will definitely take you to where Haruto is!

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:47.580
How annoying, you bastard!

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:51.000
Rejecting my service left and right...

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:53.840
Why can't you allow me to duel happily?

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:57.630
I really want to see your painful expressions!

00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:59.850
Wha... what's wrong with that person?

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:03.890
Oh wait, I got a good idea.

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:08.400
If you don't like the previous services, then allow me to introduce other "services" to you!

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:10.440
You will definitely like this!

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:18.820
This is...

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:24.490
Haruto...

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:26.830
Haruto!

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:29.880
That's the 'life' of your cute brother.

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:33.880
What are you guys doing to Haruto?!

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:35.800
Oh... I have no idea...

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:38.840
But I do know my big brother's character is even more shameless than mine.

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:42.510
But judging from his condition, if you can't stop it quick enough, it's gonna be bad...

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:44.100
Brother...

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:46.060
You bastard!

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:50.440
Your expression is really nice, Kaito! 
See, you can do it if you try.

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:55.030
Seeing your prideful expression became twisted is such an irresistible joy!

00:18:58.070 --> 00:18:58.900
Unforgivable!

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:05.790
Just summon it, summon your ace!

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:08.080
That moment will be your last, Kaito!

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:11.750
My turn, draw!

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:14.170
Hey, Kaito, calm yourself!

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:16.920
I summon Photon Slasher!

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:26.310
Then at this moment, Photon Pressure World's effect activates!

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:29.180
When a photon monster was summoned,

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:35.900
players who do not control a photon monster will receive damage equal to the level of the summoned monster x 100!

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:42.740
I will annihilate anyone who dares to stop me!

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:44.280
Kaito...

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:48.500
Now there are 2 monsters with 2000 or more ATK on Kaito's field.

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:54.750
I release Photon Crusher with 2000 ATK and Photon Slasher with 2100 ATK,

00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:03.840
The galaxy that shines within the darkness now become the light of hope, and serve under my command!

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:06.810
The embodiment of light , descend now!

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:11.440
Come forth! Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon!

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:14.190
So it finally appears...

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:17.110
So that's the legendary Galaxy-Eyes!

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:19.400
But everything is going according to our calculations.

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:20.440
Time to assault.

00:20:21.190 --> 00:20:22.780
I got it, brother.

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:30.500
This is bad... Photon Pressure World's effect will activate once again!

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:44.010
Go, Galaxy-Eyes, attack Giant Killer!

00:20:45.050 --> 00:20:47.720
Photon Stream of Destruction!

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:49.350
You fell for it, Kaito!

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:54.060
Permanent Trap activate! Stonehenge Shield!

00:20:55.100 --> 00:21:01.650
This card negates the attack from a monster with 3000 or more original attack,

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:06.160
its ATK will become zero, and its effect will also be negated!

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:16.710
What did you say?

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:20.420
Now Galaxy Eyes's ATK become zero.

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:23.260
And its monster effect will also be negated.

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:26.260
A trap that foresees Galaxy Eyes's ability!

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:27.720
So all this was a trap?

00:21:28.090 --> 00:21:31.060
OOPArts monster Masshu Maccu's effect activates!

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:35.890
With Masshu Maccu, when a monster on the field changes its ATK,

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:41.530
by detaching 1 overlay unit, it can inflict damage to my opponent equal to the changed amount!

00:21:42.690 --> 00:21:44.110
Go, Masshu Maccu!

00:21:44.690 --> 00:21:46.280
Infinity Cannon!

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:53.250
Your Galaxy Eyes changes its ATK from 3000 to 0,

00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:55.330
It's over, Kaito.

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:58.120
Take 3000 damage!

00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:01.290
Kaito!

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:23.070
<i>Someone gave me some water.</i>

00:22:23.440 --> 00:22:28.990
<i>So I was able to paint a rainbow with ease.</i>

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:34.910
<i>I want to become someone perfect.</i>

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:37.960
<i>But it's very difficult.</i>

00:22:38.960 --> 00:22:41.540
<i>Even with me suffering,</i>

00:22:41.670 --> 00:22:45.630
<i>I can't seem to grasp victory.</i>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:48.430
<i>I want to bloom!</i>

00:22:48.970 --> 00:22:52.890
<i>I must be having some kind of weird dream.</i>

00:22:52.890 --> 00:22:55.930
<i>But If I must fulfill this,</i>

00:22:56.430 --> 00:22:59.230
<i>Then I don't mind being laughed at for it.</i>

00:22:59.390 --> 00:23:06.320
<i>Since it's because your limits are decided on your own.</i>

00:23:06.610 --> 00:23:09.360
<i>I'll show it, overcoming it to tomorrow.</i>

00:23:09.610 --> 00:23:13.830
<i>Ah, I'm aiming for the big blue sky.</i>

00:23:14.030 --> 00:23:15.790
<i>For all of its glory.</i>

00:23:15.790 --> 00:23:17.580
<i>The Freesia of Desire.</i>

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:22.960
<i>All of those countless flower petals</i>

00:23:23.170 --> 00:23:26.000
<i>They came at the expense of</i>

00:23:26.840 --> 00:23:29.590
<i>me being able to reach those heights.</i>

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:34.010
<i>Ah, even though I lost my way today,</i>

00:23:34.180 --> 00:23:35.850
<i>I still yearn for it.</i>

00:23:35.850 --> 00:23:38.140
<i>That Freesia of Desire.</i>

00:23:40.270 --> 00:23:44.400
After seeing Haruto's painful expressions, Kaito's dueling finally start to crumble.

00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:47.860
Thus we were pushed to the corner by IV and III's strategy,

00:23:48.900 --> 00:23:49.950
Calm down, Kaito!

00:23:50.200 --> 00:23:51.400
What's that light?

00:23:51.780 --> 00:23:54.990
Now a new power will be entrusted to his deck!

00:23:55.410 --> 00:23:56.620
Don't give up, Kaito!

00:23:57.200 --> 00:24:00.790
If you don't protect Haruto, then who will?

00:24:01.540 --> 00:24:03.120
Next time in Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal:

00:24:03.330 --> 00:24:07.000
The Miraculous Overlay, Neo Galaxy Eyes Photon Dragon!

00:24:07.420 --> 00:24:08.960
I'll gonna bring it to 'em!
